    "question": {
      ":question/id": "52ea580a-6917-571f-8874-292362816452",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Express $8\\sin^4\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{5}\\right)-8\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{5}\\right)+1$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Write $u=\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{5}\\right)$. Expanding the square gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(1-2u)^2-1 &=8u^2-8u+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRegroup the given expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&8\\sin^4\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{5}\\right)-8\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{5}\\right)+1\\\\&\\qquad=2\\left(1-2\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{5}\\right)\\right)^2-1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse $1-2\\sin^2 x=\\cos(2x)$ on the inner expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n1-2\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{5}\\right)&=\\cos\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{5}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute, then apply the cosine form once more:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&2\\left(1-2\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{5}\\right)\\right)^2-1\\\\&\\qquad=2\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{5}\\right)-1\\\\&\\qquad=\\cos\\left(\\frac{4\\pi}{5}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
