      ":question/worked-solution": "Write $u=\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{15}\\right)$. Expanding the square gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(2u-1)^2-1 &=8u^2-8u+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRegroup the given expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&8\\cos^4\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{15}\\right)-8\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{15}\\right)+1\\\\&\\qquad=2\\left(2\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{15}\\right)-1\\right)^2-1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse $2\\cos^2 x-1=\\cos(2x)$ on the inner expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{15}\\right)-1&=\\cos\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{15}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute, then apply the cosine form once more:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&2\\left(2\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{15}\\right)-1\\right)^2-1\\\\&\\qquad=2\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{15}\\right)-1\\\\&\\qquad=\\cos\\left(\\frac{4\\pi}{15}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
